# Lint configuration.
#
# Lint stays enabled and fatal: a lint error fails CI, exactly as a compile
# error does. These two checks are disabled for stated reasons, not to make the
# build green.
#
#  - GradleDependency: "a newer version exists" is not a defect. AndroidX
#    versions are pinned deliberately to a combination verified to build
#    together; upgrading them one at a time because lint suggested it is how a
#    Compose project acquires an unresolvable dependency graph.
#
#  - OldTargetApi: the target SDK (35) is chosen for the POCO X3 Pro running
#    Android 13; lint's suggestion to chase a newer platform each time it ships
#    would silently change runtime behaviour on the user's device.
#
# Everything else — including Compose correctness checks such as
# ProduceStateDoesNotAssignValue, accessibility and scoped-storage rules — is
# reported and still fails the build.
lint {
    disable += setOf("GradleDependency", "OldTargetApi")
    abortOnError = true
    checkDependencies = false
}
